<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="4"><strong>HUMOR-</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><strong></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><strong><font face="Arial,
sans-serif">Feed My Cow</font></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><strong><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2"><span>One Sunday a cowboy went to church.
When he entered, he saw that he and the preacher were the only ones
present. The preacher asked the cowboy if he wanted him to go ahead and
preach.</span></font></font></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><strong><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2"><span>The cowboy said, &quot;I'm not too
smart, but if I went to feed my cattle and only one showed up, I'd feed
him.&quot;</span></font></font></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><strong><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2"><span>So the minister began his
sermon.</span></font></font></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><strong><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2"><span>One hour passed, then two hours,
then two-and-a-half hours. The preacher finally finished and came down to
ask the cowboy how he had liked the
sermon.</span></font></font></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><strong><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2"><span>The cowboy answered slowly,
&quot;Well, I'm not very smart, but if I went to feed my cattle and only
one showed up, I sure wouldn't feed him ALL the
hay.&quot;</span></font></font></strong></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><strong><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2"><span>.....Rodney and Jean Francis (gfm@xtra.co.nz)
</span></font></font></strong><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">by way of &ldquo;Christian Voices&rdquo; (</font></font><font
color="#0000ff"><u><a href="http://www.christianvoicesworldwide.com/"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">www.ChristianVoicesWorldwide.com</font></font></a></u></font><font
color="#000000"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">)</font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>THOUGHT PROVOKING &ndash;
INSPIRATIONAL</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><strong>Are You Listening?</strong></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">During my young adult years, I can
remember getting phone calls that turned out being a little
frustrating.&nbsp; The caller--a friend or even close relative--would greet
me, get my cheerful, brief response and then begin to talk...and talk...and
talk.&nbsp; </font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">I would get a phoned diatribe about the
latest crisis, the latest problems, or a resume of recent events and
activities.&nbsp; I would suitably murmur brief responses and listen...and
listen...and listen.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">As the speaker would finish the long
monologue, I'd think, &quot;Ah ha, now I'll get the chance to share a
bit!&quot;&nbsp; No such luck!&nbsp; The caller would have to go, had a
million things to do, or (if long distance) didn't want to run up too big a
bill.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">I'd wish these callers a brief, cheerful
farewell, adding best wishes when able, hang up, and sigh.&nbsp; There was
just no getting many words in edgewise.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Sometimes our prayers to God are just like
the &quot;monologue phone calls.&quot;&nbsp; Rather than being an exchange
between friends, with genuine communication and sharing, our prayers become
long monologues of petition, complaint, or bargaining.&nbsp; Rather than
going on and on, we need to pause, to listen, and respect the Lord Most
High.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">We also need to add our love, our praise,
our thanksgiving, our joyous appreciation of all the good that God
gives.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">When was the last time you complained
about not getting an answer to prayer?&nbsp; Were you truly
listening?&nbsp; </font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">In the quiet, God's gentle answers of yes,
no, or maybe later will sound in the calmness of mind and heart.&nbsp; Try
listening!</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">.....Mary-Ellen Grisham - </font></font><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2">Eternal_Ink (</font></font><font
color="#0000ff"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2"><u>meginrose@charter.net</u></font></font></font><font
